        <item>
            <title>0.18.28</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:16:45 +0100</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>0.18.28</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.18.28</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>What's new in 0.18.28</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>App volume explains itself</strong> — rest the pointer on an App volume dial and a short card says what it does: it turns the volume of the app under the pointer. The card shows three times at most and stops once you turned the dial.</li>
<li><strong>New installs</strong> — the starter menu has an App volume dial beside Volume.</li>
<li><strong>A blocked App volume dial says so</strong> — when macOS has not allowed Rayto to change an app&#x27;s volume, the dial shows a red crossed speaker and does not turn. A card with <strong>Open Settings</strong> takes you to the switch. An app no longer goes silent without a word.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
